Two files created:

**`ErrorBoundary.tsx`** — the component itself:
- `getDerivedStateFromError` captures the error into state, triggering the fallback render
- `componentDidCatch` logs full details (`message`, `stack`, `componentStack`) and forwards to an optional `onError` prop
- Accepts an optional `fallback` render prop for custom UI; otherwise shows `DefaultFallback`
- `reset` clears the error state, letting children re-mount on the next render

**`ErrorBoundary.test.tsx`** — covers the key behaviors

**Usage:**

```tsx
// Basic — uses built-in fallback UI
<ErrorBoundary onError={(err, info) => reportToSentry(err, info)}>
  <YourComponent />
</ErrorBoundary>

// Custom fallback UI
<ErrorBoundary fallback={(error, reset) => (
  <MyToast message={error.message} onRetry={reset} />
)}>
  <YourComponent />
</ErrorBoundary>
```

**Props:**

| Prop | Type | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `children` | `ReactNode` | Components to protect |
| `fallback` | `(error, reset) => ReactNode` | Custom fallback renderer |
| `onError` | `(error, info) => void` | Hook for external logging (Sentry, etc.) |
